{"id":"twitter:1715414670100529411","tweet_id":"1715414670100529411","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1715414670100529411","title":"@Doug_Lemov agree which is why strategy instruction has lower effects with skilled readers. Once you internalize vocabulary strategies become automate","summary":"@Doug_Lemov agree which is why strategy instruction has lower effects with skilled readers. Once you internalize vocabulary strategies become automated skills. Ex Teaching folks to read context clues has ceiling. strategy instruction with students with IEP language goals higher effect","date":"2023-10-20","published":"2023-10-20T17:08:22+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/Doug_Lemov/status/1715384794303832079","reply_tweet_id":"1715384794303832079","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Doug_Lemov agree which is why strategy instruction has lower effects with skilled readers.<br><br>Once you internalize vocabulary strategies become automated skills.<br><br>Ex Teaching folks to read context clues has ceiling.<br><br>strategy instruction with students with IEP language goals higher effect</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1715414670100529411","display_date":"October 20, 2023 · 17:08 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1715413871656386648","tweet_id":"1715413871656386648","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1715413871656386648","title":"@edelman_vincent @Doug_Lemov No, which is always been a crux, but also means we use vocabulary tools as a proxy for background knowledge and or compre","summary":"@edelman_vincent @Doug_Lemov No, which is always been a crux, but also means we use vocabulary tools as a proxy for background knowledge and or comprehension measures in many studies. And there is no such thing as a vocabulary intervention to replace reading and writing. Heart of the Mathew Effect","date":"2023-10-20","published":"2023-10-20T17:05:12+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/i/status/1715405572164469241","reply_tweet_id":"1715405572164469241","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@edelman_vincent @Doug_Lemov No, which is always been a crux, but also means we use vocabulary tools as a proxy for background knowledge and or comprehension measures in many studies.<br><br>And there is no such thing as a vocabulary intervention to replace reading and writing.<br><br>Heart of the Mathew Effect</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1715413871656386648","display_date":"October 20, 2023 · 17:05 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
