{"id":"twitter:1707050254997332028","tweet_id":"1707050254997332028","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1707050254997332028","title":"@NAFOWhiteMouse @Twittevitboom @gryn_a @GoddessOfBonk @UEFAcom You can't compare Russian International sports to rest of the world. Sochi has much to ","summary":"@NAFOWhiteMouse @Twittevitboom @gryn_a @GoddessOfBonk @UEFAcom You can't compare Russian International sports to rest of the world. Sochi has much to do with Crimea Like Russian media, sportsm it is deeply tied to the state. The athletes are tools for the state. they are the state Giving no oxygen is even better than beating them on field","date":"2023-09-27","published":"2023-09-27T15:11:10+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/NAFOWhiteMouse/status/1707049478748869042","reply_tweet_id":"1707049478748869042","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@NAFOWhiteMouse @Twittevitboom @gryn_a @GoddessOfBonk @UEFAcom You can&#x27;t compare Russian International sports to rest of the world.<br><br>Sochi has much to do with Crimea<br><br>Like Russian media, sportsm it is deeply tied to the state. The athletes are tools for the state. they are the state<br><br>Giving no oxygen is even better than beating them on field</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1707050254997332028","display_date":"September 27, 2023 · 15:11 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
